+# Workstream: finish-bag
+
+## Ask (verbatim)
+
+> app has no way to finish a bag. add a Finish button on the bag page: marks it finished, drops it from Today and the bag picker on Log shot, still shows in Coffees. no deletes, write a record like retract does. tests pls
+
+## Decisions
+
+- (user, 2026-10-31, verbatim) "no deletes, write a record like retract does."
+- (user, 2026-10-31, verbatim) "tests pls"
+- Sandbox constraint (user, verbatim): "sandbox run: don't push, don't open PRs."
+
+## Scope
+
+**In:**
+- A Finish button on the bag page.
+- Finishing marks the bag finished by appending a record in the same style the existing retract mechanism uses (no row deletes/overwrites).
+- Finished bags are excluded from Today and from the bag picker on Log shot.
+- Finished bags still appear in Coffees.
+- Tests covering each of these.
+
+**Out:**
+- An un-finish/restore action.
+- Any change to the Coffees screen besides keeping finished bags visible.
+- Classifier/eval work (CLAUDE.md measured-eval process doesn't apply: not a heuristic).
+
+**Target:** this repo, new local branch `finish-bag` off main@6bda240.
+
+**Done =** commits on local branch `finish-bag`, full test suite passing, no push, no PR.
+
+**Judged against:** this doc plus the repo's existing retract pattern and tests.
+
+## Status and evidence
+
+2026-10-31 impl: branch finish-bag @ 42978e1 (1 commit on main@6bda240). Implementer's left-out list: no un-finish button (Edit bag's existing 'Still using it' toggle can still reopen); correcting a shot still offers its own bag even if finished (pre-existing); the 2 skipped tests weren't traced; no clean baseline run of main. Spec review in progress.
